<section class="ac-blue section" style="padding-bottom: 80px;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Jewelry and watch retail questions, answered.</h2>
    </div>
    <div style="max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How does Teamwork Commerce track individual jewelry pieces?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Every piece is serialized as its own unit, with or without RFID. With RFID, the piece carries an EPC; without it, it carries its own unit ID. With RFID, a handheld counts a display case without handling a piece.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Does Teamwork Commerce handle repairs and appraisals?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce is not a repair or appraisal system, and it does not handle trade-ins. It integrates tightly with the systems that do. The associate takes the deposit in Teamwork Commerce, the repair goes to your repair system, and its status comes back so the customer can be told the piece is ready to collect.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Can Teamwork handle deposits, layaway and special orders?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. The platform supports deposits for custom and special orders and layaway, with automatic balance tracking and customer notifications.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          How is customer data protected?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Teamwork Commerce is SOC 2 Type 2 certified, GDPR compliant and PCI DSS compliant. Those controls exist so client details, purchase history and payment data stay protected, and they apply to every retailer on the platform, whatever the value of the merchandise. Role-based permissions control who can view customer data and process transactions.</p></div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <h3 class="faq-q"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" onclick="var i=this.closest('.faq-item');i.classList.toggle('open');this.setAttribute('aria-expanded',i.classList.contains('open'))">
          Is Teamwork Commerce built for multi-location jewelry chains?
          <span class="faq-icon"><i class="ti ti-plus"></i></span>
        </button></h3>
        <div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Teamwork Commerce is enterprise retail infrastructure for jewelry and watch chains, with experience across leading global jewelry brands. Capabilities include serialized tracking of each piece as its own unit, with or without RFID, integrated OMS for omnichannel fulfillment, SOC 2 Type 2, PCI DSS and GDPR compliance, and localization in 40+ countries with multi-currency support, so expanding into a new market is not a re-platform.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

